-- חוזר לבעלויות תשס"ט/9: תשלום דמי הבראה ומענק יובל לשנת הלימודים תשס"ט
-- Two payments for school year 2008/09 (תשס"ט). The recuperation pay, cut
-- under the 2009 temporary law on partial payment of recuperation pay in the
-- public service and the Wage Commissioner's circular 2009-1-26: the halved
-- day price, the teachers paid early, substitutes paid monthly, retirees and
-- the dead, budget pensioners, the days table, part-time and above-full
-- positions, what the cut does not touch, and who is outside the circular.
-- And the jubilee grant: who is entitled, how much, when it is paid.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common
IMPORT daydate

§ `תשס"ט/9 תשלום דמי הבראה ומענק יובל לשנת הלימודים תשס"ט`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, title, date (18.6.2009), addressee and subject line; no rule.

-- Time, where a rule has a deadline, is counted in school months from
-- September 2008 (common.l4: September = 1, so June 2009 is 10); 2010's
-- months follow on (June 2010 is 22).

§§ `1 תשלום דמי הבראה`

-- akn:art_1/p1 The lead-in: the Knesset passed on 16.6.2009 the law on partial payment of recuperation pay in the public service in 2009 and 2010; its rules for teachers are the paragraphs below.
-- akn:art_1/p2 The tail of the law's title ("(הוראת שעה), התשס"ט-2009"); no rule.
-- akn:art_1/p3 The lead-in: under that law and the Wage Commissioner's circular 2009-1-26 of 17.6.2009, adapted to teachers, recuperation pay is paid as set out below; the rules are the subparagraphs.

@desc How a teaching employee's recuperation pay reaches him, as sections 1ד, 1ה and 1ו tell them apart.
DECLARE `recuperation payment form` IS ONE OF
    @desc paid once a year, as a teacher's is, with June's salary
    `an annual payment`
    @desc a separate salary component not paid annually, e.g. a substitute teacher employed above 51 days
    `a separate component paid other than annually`
    @desc included in the regular salary, not a separate component
    `included in the regular salary`

@desc The populations of teaching employees section 1יד puts outside the circular's cut, and the rest.
DECLARE `teaching population` IS ONE OF
    @desc employed in the State service in official education (kindergartens, primary, middle, special-education schools, adult education)
    `State service in official education`
    @desc recognised unofficial education, in kindergartens, primary schools (networks included) and middle schools
    `recognised unofficial kindergartens, primary or middle schools`
    `colleges of teacher training`
    `government post-primary schools`
    @desc every other teaching employee of an owner
    `any other teaching employee of an owner`

@desc A teaching employee's recuperation pay for the determining period, as far as this circular asks.
DECLARE `recuperation case` HAS
    `teaching seniority in years`           IS A NUMBER  @desc seniority in teaching (ותק בהוראה); the first year of teaching is year 1
    `position fraction`                     IS A NUMBER  @desc the share of a full position held that year (1 = 100%), at the same employer
    `months of work in the year`            IS A NUMBER  @desc months of work that year, as section 1ט's "(1/10 לכל חודש עבודה)" counts them
    `daily price without the cut`           IS A NUMBER  @desc the price of one recuperation day that applies to this employee before any cut, shekels
    `civil-service daily price without the cut` IS A NUMBER @desc the same price for a teaching employee employed in the State service, shekels
    `form of payment`                       IS A `recuperation payment form`
    `paid in 2009 before June's salary`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc was paid recuperation pay, all or part, in 2009 before the June 2009 salary
    `budget-pension retiree entitled from the former employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc a pensioner on a budget pension entitled to recuperation pay from the former employer, for a whole year as a pensioner
    `population`                            IS A `teaching population`

DECLARE `recuperation action` IS ONE OF
    `pay recuperation pay` HAS `recuperation paid` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the withheld part after the determining period`
    `pay the cut part for the period after retirement` HAS `refund paid` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the jubilee grant` HAS `grant paid` IS A NUMBER

§§§ `1א התקופה הקובעת`

-- Section 1א: the determining period — the law applies in 2009 and 2010.
@ref akn:art_1__para_a
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the determining period` `year` IF
    `year` EQUALS 2009 OR `year` EQUALS 2010

§§§ `1ב מחיר יום הבראה`

-- Section 1ב: the price of a recuperation day, by which recuperation pay is
-- computed, is cut by 50%, so the recuperation pay the employer pays is
-- cut by that rate; so in 2009 it falls from 383 ₪ to 191.5 ₪ a day, and
-- "in any case" the cut of the day price is no more than 191.5 ₪.
@ref akn:art_1__para_b akn:art_1__para_b/p2
GIVEN `price` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the day price after the cut` `price` IS
    `price` MINUS `the cut of a day price` `price`

GIVEN `price` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the cut of a day price` `price` IS
    min (`price` TIMES `the cut rate`) `the most the 2009 cut takes from a day`

`the cut rate` MEANS 0.5
`the 2009 day price before the cut` MEANS 383
`the 2009 day price after the cut` MEANS 191.5
`the most the 2009 cut takes from a day` MEANS 191.5

§§§ `1ג–1ה מי משלם מה ומתי`

GIVEN c IS A `recuperation case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cut applies to` c IF
        c's `population` EQUALS `any other teaching employee of an owner`
    AND (NOT `the cut does not reach a budget pensioner` c)

-- The full-year recuperation pay before any cut, at a given day price.
GIVEN `price` IS A NUMBER, c IS A `recuperation case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `recuperation pay at` `price` `for` c IS
    `recuperation days` (c's `teaching seniority in years`)
    TIMES `price`
    TIMES `the share of the allowance` c

-- The 2009 annual payment (sections 1ב, 1ג, 1ז, 1יג, 1יד): cut at the
-- payment date, June, unless the employee was paid before June, or is
-- outside the cut.
@export default The recuperation pay an owner pays a teaching employee in 2009 under circular תשס"ט/9, after the cut of the 2009 temporary law
GIVEN c IS A `recuperation case` @desc the employee's recuperation case
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `recuperation pay in 2009` c IS
    IF `the cut applies to` c AND NOT `the 2009 payment is left uncut` c
    THEN `recuperation pay at` (`the day price after the cut` (c's `daily price without the cut`)) `for` c
    ELSE `recuperation pay at` (c's `daily price without the cut`) `for` c

-- Section 1ג: an employee paid recuperation pay, all or part, in 2009
-- before June's salary is paid none in 2010, and what he was paid in 2009
-- is not cut; except that one entitled to more than the civil service's day
-- price is paid in 2010 at a day price equal to the difference between the
-- two uncut prices (none where it is not more).
@ref akn:art_1__para_c
GIVEN c IS A `recuperation case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2009 payment is left uncut` c IF
    c's `paid in 2009 before June's salary`

@ref akn:art_1__para_c
GIVEN c IS A `recuperation case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2010 day price for one paid early in 2009` c IS
    max (c's `daily price without the cut` MINUS c's `civil-service daily price without the cut`) 0

-- Section 1ג's own example: a day price of 500 ₪ for the teacher and of
-- 400 ₪ in the civil service. The clause stating the example's result is
-- printed with its figures reordered ("בסך ₪ 500( ₪ 100 פחות. )₪ 400",
-- MMS-426), so the day price the example arrives at is not something the
-- corpus text says: it is a named input until the corpus is fixed and
-- re-synced. The assert below checks the rule's own arithmetic on the
-- example's premises, which the corpus prints whole.
@ref akn:art_1__para_c/p2
`the section 1ג example` MEANS
    `recuperation case` WITH
        `teaching seniority in years`           IS 12
        `position fraction`                     IS 1
        `months of work in the year`            IS 10
        `daily price without the cut`           IS 500
        `civil-service daily price without the cut` IS 400
        `form of payment`                       IS `an annual payment`
        `paid in 2009 before June's salary`     IS TRUE
        `budget-pension retiree entitled from the former employer` IS FALSE
        `population`                            IS `any other teaching employee of an owner`

#ASSERT `the 2010 day price for one paid early in 2009` `the section 1ג example` EQUALS 500 MINUS 400

@desc Circular 2008-09/9, section 1ג's example: the day price at which its teacher is paid in 2010, as the example states it. The corpus prints this clause scrambled (MMS-426), so the value is supplied from outside until the corpus is fixed and re-synced.
ASSUME `the day price section 1ג's example states` IS A NUMBER

-- Whether the rule meets the example's stated result; not asserted while
-- that result is an input.
`the rule gives section 1ג's example its stated day price` MEANS
    `the 2010 day price for one paid early in 2009` `the section 1ג example` EQUALS `the day price section 1ג's example states`

-- Section 1ד: an employee whose recuperation pay is a separate component not
-- paid annually (e.g. a substitute above 51 days) is treated ONLY as follows,
-- for the 2010 payments, month by month of calendar 2010:
-- (1) employed by the employer all of 2009: none in 2010;
-- (2) employed part of 2009: none in a first stretch of 2010 as long as the
--     time employed in 2009, then cut by half to the end of 2010;
-- (3) not employed by the employer in 2009: cut by half in 2010.
@ref akn:art_1__para_d akn:art_1__para_d__subpara_1 akn:art_1__para_d__subpara_2 akn:art_1__para_d__subpara_3
GIVEN `months employed in 2009` IS A NUMBER, `month of 2010` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `share of the 2010 component paid` `months employed in 2009` `month of 2010` IS
    BRANCH IF `months employed in 2009` AT LEAST 12 THEN 0
           IF `month of 2010` AT MOST `months employed in 2009` THEN 0
           OTHERWISE 1 MINUS `the cut rate`

-- Section 1ד(2)'s own example: five months in 2009 — nothing in 2010's first
-- five months, half thereafter.
@ref akn:art_1__para_d__subpara_2/p2
`the section 1ד example holds` MEANS
        all (GIVEN k YIELD `share of the 2010 component paid` 5 k EQUALS 0) (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5)
    AND all (GIVEN k YIELD `share of the 2010 component paid` 5 k EQUALS 0.5) (LIST 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12)
#ASSERT `the section 1ד example holds`

-- Section 1ה: where recuperation pay is included in the regular salary, the
-- 2010 salary is cut by instructions to be published separately. The cut
-- for them is not set here; it is an input of those instructions.
@ref akn:art_1__para_e
GIVEN c IS A `recuperation case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cut is set by separate instructions for` c IF
    c's `form of payment` EQUALS `included in the regular salary`

§§§ `1ו עובד הוראה שפרש או נפטר במהלך שנת הבראה`

-- Section 1ו(1): a teaching employee, or former one, paid recuperation pay
-- annually in the determining period, who retired or died, and who (or his
-- survivor, family member or estate) is entitled to recuperation pay from
-- the former employer also for the time after the retirement or death, has
-- the cut applied only to the part of the recuperation year BEFORE that
-- date, under sections ב–ו.
@ref akn:art_1__para_f akn:art_1__para_f__subpara_1
GIVEN c IS A `recuperation case`, `share of the year before the retirement or death` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `recuperation pay for a retiree's year` c `share of the year before the retirement or death` IS
    `recuperation pay at` (`the day price after the cut` (c's `daily price without the cut`)) `for` c
        TIMES `share of the year before the retirement or death`
    PLUS (`recuperation pay at` (c's `daily price without the cut`) `for` c
          TIMES (1 MINUS `share of the year before the retirement or death`))

-- Section 1ו(1), second paragraph: "שנת הבראה" is a year — "meaning the
-- school year from 1.9.08 to 31.8.09" — for all or part of which recuperation
-- pay is paid whose payment date falls in the determining period. The
-- parenthesis names 2008/09 alone, while the determining period runs into
-- 2010, whose June payment is for 2009/10 (F-2008-09_tashsat_09-b). The
-- reading adopted: the definition's general words govern — a recuperation
-- year is the school year a payment in the determining period is for,
-- 2009/10 included — and the parenthesis names the one this circular pays.
@ref akn:art_1__para_f__subpara_1/p2
GIVEN `school year ends in` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a recuperation year` `school year ends in` IF
    `in the determining period` `school year ends in`

`the recuperation year's first day` MEANS Date 1 9 2008
`the recuperation year's last day` MEANS Date 31 8 2009

GIVEN `day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the recuperation year as defined` `day` IF
    `day` AT LEAST `the recuperation year's first day` AND `day` AT MOST `the recuperation year's last day`

-- Section 1ו(2): where the retirement or death comes after the payment
-- date of the year's recuperation pay, the employer pays the entitled
-- person the part cut (if any) for the period after it, under sections
-- ב–ו, within 60 days of the retirement or death. This rule runs on its
-- own timeline, in days from the retirement or death.
@ref akn:art_1__para_f__subpara_2
GIVEN c IS A `recuperation case`, `share of the year after the retirement or death` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `recuperation action`
DECIDE `refund within 60 days` c `share of the year after the retirement or death` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `pay the cut part for the period after retirement` `refund`
          PROVIDED `refund` AT LEAST `the cut part for the period after retirement` c `share of the year after the retirement or death`
    WITHIN 60
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "section 1ו(2): the part cut for the period after retirement or death is paid within 60 days of it"

GIVEN c IS A `recuperation case`, `share of the year after the retirement or death` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the cut part for the period after retirement` c `share of the year after the retirement or death` IS
    (`recuperation pay at` (c's `daily price without the cut`) `for` c
     MINUS `recuperation pay at` (`the day price after the cut` (c's `daily price without the cut`)) `for` c)
    TIMES `share of the year after the retirement or death`

§§§ `1ז גמלאים בפנסיה תקציבית`

-- Section 1ז: the cut of sections ב–ו does not apply to budget pensioners
-- entitled to a recuperation allowance from their former employer.
@ref akn:art_1__para_g
GIVEN c IS A `recuperation case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cut does not reach a budget pensioner` c IF
    c's `budget-pension retiree entitled from the former employer`

-- Section 1ז, second sentence: for one entitled in 2009 and/or 2010 to the
-- allowance for a year partly active and partly a budget pensioner, section
-- 1ו governs, i.e. the cut falls on the active part.
@ref akn:art_1__para_g
GIVEN c IS A `recuperation case`, `share of the year active` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `recuperation pay for a year partly as a budget pensioner` c `share of the year active` IS
    `recuperation pay for a retiree's year` c `share of the year active`

§§§ `1ח טבלת ימי ההבראה`

-- Section 1ח's table, in the printed order. "3 שנים ראשונות" is years 1 to
-- 3; "25 ומעלה" has no upper bound (999).
@ref akn:art_1__para_h akn:art_1__para_h/p2 akn:art_1__para_h/p3 akn:art_1__para_h/p4 akn:art_1__para_h/p5 akn:art_1__para_h/p6 akn:art_1__para_h/p7 akn:art_1__para_h/p8
`the table of recuperation days` MEANS
    LIST `seniority band` 1  3   7,
         `seniority band` 4  10  9,
         `seniority band` 11 15  10,
         `seniority band` 16 19  11,
         `seniority band` 20 24  12,
         `seniority band` 25 999 13

DECLARE `seniority band` HAS
    `from seniority`  IS A NUMBER
    `to seniority`    IS A NUMBER
    `days of the band` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the days the table gives for year` n IS
    map (GIVEN b YIELD b's `days of the band`)
        (filter (GIVEN b YIELD n AT LEAST b's `from seniority` AND n AT MOST b's `to seniority`)
                `the table of recuperation days`)

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `recuperation days` n IS
    BRANCH IF n AT LEAST 25 THEN 13
           IF n AT LEAST 20 THEN 12
           IF n AT LEAST 16 THEN 11
           IF n AT LEAST 11 THEN 10
           IF n AT LEAST 4  THEN 9
           IF n AT LEAST 1  THEN 7
           OTHERWISE 0

§§§ `1ט–1י משרה חלקית ומשרה מעל שלמה`

-- Section 1ט: a part-time employee is entitled to the allowance "in
-- proportion to the part of his position that year (1/10 for each month of
-- work)". The sentence pro-rates by position, its parenthesis by months
-- (F-2008-09_tashsat_09-a). The reading adopted: both — the position share
-- (capped by section 1י) times the months share, the months share no more
-- than a whole year.
@ref akn:art_1__para_i
GIVEN c IS A `recuperation case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the share of the allowance` c IS
    `the position counted` c
    TIMES min (`share by the months, as the parenthesis says` c) 1

GIVEN c IS A `recuperation case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `share by the position, as the sentence says` c IS
    min (c's `position fraction`) 1

GIVEN c IS A `recuperation case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `share by the months, as the parenthesis says` c IS
    c's `months of work in the year` TIMES 0.1

-- Section 1י: one employed above a full position at one employer is
-- entitled to the allowance of one full position only.
@ref akn:art_1__para_j
GIVEN c IS A `recuperation case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position counted` c IS
    min (c's `position fraction`) 1

§§§ `1יא–1יד`

@desc The matters section 1יא computes as if the recuperation pay had been paid in full.
DECLARE `computation` IS ONE OF
    `the sum paid to a provident fund, pension fund and study fund included`
    `income and tax on provident-fund payments in the determining period`
    `budget-pension payments`
    `one-off payments on the end of employment`
    `the determining salary for the 2% budget-pension deduction`
    `any other computation`

-- Section 1יא: for the five matters it lists, the recuperation pay is
-- reckoned as paid in full, without the cut. Item (2)'s
-- sections of the Income Tax Ordinance are printed with their numbers
-- reordered (MMS-426); the matter is encoded by what it is, and no section
-- number is taken from it.
@ref akn:art_1__para_ja akn:art_1__para_ja__subpara_1 akn:art_1__para_ja__subpara_2 akn:art_1__para_ja__subpara_2/p2 akn:art_1__para_ja__subpara_3 akn:art_1__para_ja__subpara_4 akn:art_1__para_ja__subpara_5 akn:art_1__para_ja__subpara_5/p2 akn:art_1__para_ja__subpara_5/p3
GIVEN c IS A `recuperation case`, `for` IS A `computation`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `recuperation pay reckoned` c `for` IS
    IF `for` EQUALS `any other computation`
    THEN `recuperation pay in 2009` c
    ELSE `recuperation pay at` (c's `daily price without the cut`) `for` c

-- Section 1יב: the part of the recuperation pay or salary not paid under
-- this circular is not paid even after the determining period. No time
-- limit: the prohibition stands.
@ref akn:art_1__para_jb
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `recuperation action`
DECIDE `the withheld part is never paid` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    SHANT `pay the withheld part after the determining period`
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "section 1יב: the part not paid under this circular is not paid even after the determining period"

-- Section 1יג: the cut is made on the date recuperation pay is paid, for
-- teachers the June salary.
@ref akn:art_1__para_jc
GIVEN c IS A `recuperation case`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `recuperation action`
DECIDE `recuperation pay with June 2009's salary` c IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `pay recuperation pay` `amount paid`
          PROVIDED `amount paid` AT LEAST `recuperation pay in 2009` c
    WITHIN `month number` June
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "section 1יג: recuperation pay, cut, is paid with June's salary"

-- Section 1יד: the circular's cut does not apply to the four populations it
-- lists (the `the cut applies to` rule above reads them off `population`).
@ref akn:art_1__para_jd akn:art_1__para_jd__subpara_1 akn:art_1__para_jd__subpara_2 akn:art_1__para_jd__subpara_3 akn:art_1__para_jd__subpara_4
`the populations outside the circular` MEANS
    LIST `State service in official education`,
         `recognised unofficial kindergartens, primary or middle schools`,
         `colleges of teacher training`,
         `government post-primary schools`

§§ `2 תשלום מענק יובל`

@desc A teaching employee's case for the jubilee grant paid in June 2009.
DECLARE `jubilee case` HAS
    `teaching seniority set in September 2008`       IS A NUMBER @desc accumulated teaching seniority, military service included, as set for the employee in September 2008
    `teaching seniority completed by 1 June 2009`    IS A NUMBER @desc the same seniority, as completed by 1 June 2009
    `years of work in Israel completed by 1 June 2009` IS A NUMBER @desc years of work in Israel, compulsory IDF service included, completed by 1 June 2009
    `unpaid-leave years with pension rights bought`  IS A NUMBER @desc years of unpaid leave for which pension rights were bought from the State or the teachers' pension funds
    `determining salary for pension and severance`   IS A NUMBER @desc the monthly determining salary for pension and severance pay, once-a-year payments such as clothing and recuperation excluded, shekels
    `jubilee position fraction`                      IS A NUMBER @desc the share of a full position held that year
    `share of the year employed`                     IS A NUMBER @desc the share of the year the employee was employed (1 = all of it)

`the jubilee threshold` MEANS 30

-- Section 2 ¶1: the grant is paid, to those entitled, with the June 2009
-- salary.
@ref akn:art_2/p1
GIVEN j IS A `jubilee case`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `recuperation action`
DECIDE `the jubilee grant with June's salary` j IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `pay the jubilee grant` `grant`
          PROVIDED `grant` AT LEAST `the jubilee grant` j
    WITHIN `month number` June
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "section 2: the jubilee grant is paid with the June 2009 salary"

-- Section 2 ¶2: the grant is paid to a teacher with accumulated teaching
-- seniority of 30 years or more, military service included, with the
-- employers, the owning bodies and formal education institutions; 2א: a
-- year of unpaid leave for which pension rights were bought counts in the
-- years of seniority. The reading adopted (F-2008-09_tashsat_09-c, -d):
-- section 2's own measure, completed by section 2ב's day, 1 June of the year.
-- F-2008-09_tashsat_09-e: "30 שנה ומעלה" or once, in the year the 30 are
-- completed (2ב's "באותה שנה"). The reading adopted: once — seniority on
-- 1 June within a year of 30 — as F-2006-07_tashsaz_06-d and
-- F-2007-08_tashsach_05-c read the same words.
@ref akn:art_2/p2 akn:art_2__para_a
GIVEN j IS A `jubilee case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the jubilee grant` j IF
        `the years counted for the jubilee` j AT LEAST `the jubilee threshold`
    AND `the years counted for the jubilee` j LESS THAN `the jubilee threshold` PLUS 1

GIVEN j IS A `jubilee case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the years counted for the jubilee` j IS
    j's `teaching seniority completed by 1 June 2009` PLUS j's `unpaid-leave years with pension rights bought`

-- Section 2 ¶2's own words, "30 שנה ומעלה", with no year named.
@ref akn:art_2/p2
GIVEN j IS A `jubilee case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has the "30 years and more" section 2 names` j IF
    `the years counted for the jubilee` j AT LEAST `the jubilee threshold`

-- Section 2 ¶3 and 2ג: 60% of the determining salary for pension and
-- severance, once-a-year payments such as clothing and recuperation
-- excluded, by the position that year up to one position, and by the share
-- of the period employed.
@ref akn:art_2/p3 akn:art_2__para_c
@export The jubilee grant an owner pays a teaching employee with the June 2009 salary under circular תשס"ט/9
GIVEN j IS A `jubilee case` @desc the employee's jubilee case
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the jubilee grant` j IS
    IF `entitled to the jubilee grant` j
    THEN `the jubilee rate`
         TIMES j's `determining salary for pension and severance`
         TIMES min (j's `jubilee position fraction`) 1
         TIMES j's `share of the year employed`
    ELSE 0

`the jubilee rate` MEANS 0.6

-- Section 2 ¶4: the grant is given by the seniority set for the employee in
-- the September of the year before the grant (F-2008-09_tashsat_09-c).
@ref akn:art_2/p4
GIVEN j IS A `jubilee case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled by the seniority set in September 2008` j IF
    j's `teaching seniority set in September 2008` PLUS j's `unpaid-leave years with pension rights bought`
    AT LEAST `the jubilee threshold`

-- akn:art_2/p5 The heading "הבהרות" over sections 2א–2ג; no rule.

-- Section 2ב: one who completed 30 years of work in Israel, compulsory IDF
-- service included, by 1 June of the year is entitled to the grant that
-- year (F-2008-09_tashsat_09-c, -d).
@ref akn:art_2__para_b
GIVEN j IS A `jubilee case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled by work in Israel completed by 1 June` j IF
    j's `years of work in Israel completed by 1 June 2009` PLUS j's `unpaid-leave years with pension rights bought`
    AT LEAST `the jubilee threshold`

-- akn:art_3 The contact line for questions (the conditions-of-service unit's telephones); no rule.

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off and signature; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- Section 1ב on the 2009 prices; a higher day price loses no more than
-- 191.5 ₪ a day.
#ASSERT `the day price after the cut` `the 2009 day price before the cut` EQUALS `the 2009 day price after the cut`
#ASSERT `the day price after the cut` 500 EQUALS 308.5

-- The printed days table is a function on years 1 to 40, and the BRANCH
-- agrees with it.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN n YIELD `the days the table gives for year` n EQUALS LIST (`recuperation days` n))
            (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 10, 11, 15, 16, 19, 20, 24, 25, 26, 30, 40)

#ASSERT `share of the 2010 component paid` 12 3 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `share of the 2010 component paid` 0 1 EQUALS 0.5

-- F-2008-09_tashsat_09-b: the June 2010 payment is in the determining
-- period, but its school year is outside the definition's parenthesis.
`the June 2010 payment is in the determining period but its school year is outside the definition` MEANS
        `in the determining period` 2010
    AND (NOT (`in the recuperation year as defined` (Date 1 3 2010)))
#ASSERT `the June 2010 payment is in the determining period but its school year is outside the definition`

-- F-2008-09_tashsat_09-a: the sentence and its parenthesis pro-rate by
-- different measures: a half-position teacher who worked all ten months
-- gets half under the one and the whole under the other, and twelve months
-- of work make more than a whole year at 1/10 a month.
`a half-position teacher for ten months` MEANS
    `recuperation case` WITH
        `teaching seniority in years`           IS 12
        `position fraction`                     IS 0.5
        `months of work in the year`            IS 10
        `daily price without the cut`           IS 383
        `civil-service daily price without the cut` IS 383
        `form of payment`                       IS `an annual payment`
        `paid in 2009 before June's salary`     IS FALSE
        `budget-pension retiree entitled from the former employer` IS FALSE
        `population`                            IS `any other teaching employee of an owner`

`a full-position teacher for twelve months` MEANS
    `recuperation case` WITH
        `teaching seniority in years`           IS 12
        `position fraction`                     IS 1
        `months of work in the year`            IS 12
        `daily price without the cut`           IS 383
        `civil-service daily price without the cut` IS 383
        `form of payment`                       IS `an annual payment`
        `paid in 2009 before June's salary`     IS FALSE
        `budget-pension retiree entitled from the former employer` IS FALSE
        `population`                            IS `any other teaching employee of an owner`

`the position and the months give different shares` MEANS
        (NOT (`share by the position, as the sentence says` `a half-position teacher for ten months`
              EQUALS `share by the months, as the parenthesis says` `a half-position teacher for ten months`))
    AND `share by the months, as the parenthesis says` `a full-position teacher for twelve months` GREATER THAN 1
#ASSERT `the position and the months give different shares`

-- F-2008-09_tashsat_09-c: two dates for the 30 years.
`a teacher who reaches 30 years in March 2009` MEANS
    `jubilee case` WITH
        `teaching seniority set in September 2008`       IS 29
        `teaching seniority completed by 1 June 2009`    IS 30
        `years of work in Israel completed by 1 June 2009` IS 30
        `unpaid-leave years with pension rights bought`  IS 0
        `determining salary for pension and severance`   IS 10000
        `jubilee position fraction`                      IS 1
        `share of the year employed`                     IS 1

`the September and the June dates give different answers` MEANS
        `entitled by work in Israel completed by 1 June` `a teacher who reaches 30 years in March 2009`
    AND (NOT (`entitled by the seniority set in September 2008` `a teacher who reaches 30 years in March 2009`))
#ASSERT `the September and the June dates give different answers`

-- F-2008-09_tashsat_09-d: two measures for the 30 years.
`a teacher with 25 years of teaching and 31 of work in Israel` MEANS
    `jubilee case` WITH
        `teaching seniority set in September 2008`       IS 25
        `teaching seniority completed by 1 June 2009`    IS 25
        `years of work in Israel completed by 1 June 2009` IS 31
        `unpaid-leave years with pension rights bought`  IS 0
        `determining salary for pension and severance`   IS 10000
        `jubilee position fraction`                      IS 1
        `share of the year employed`                     IS 1

`teaching seniority and work in Israel give different answers` MEANS
        `entitled by work in Israel completed by 1 June` `a teacher with 25 years of teaching and 31 of work in Israel`
    AND (NOT (`entitled to the jubilee grant` `a teacher with 25 years of teaching and 31 of work in Israel`))
#ASSERT `teaching seniority and work in Israel give different answers`

-- Worked examples, on the circular's own 2009 prices; the salary figures
-- are round placeholders.
`a full-position teacher in year 22` MEANS
    `recuperation case` WITH
        `teaching seniority in years`           IS 22
        `position fraction`                     IS 1
        `months of work in the year`            IS 10
        `daily price without the cut`           IS 383
        `civil-service daily price without the cut` IS 383
        `form of payment`                       IS `an annual payment`
        `paid in 2009 before June's salary`     IS FALSE
        `budget-pension retiree entitled from the former employer` IS FALSE
        `population`                            IS `any other teaching employee of an owner`

`a teacher in a government post-primary school` MEANS
    `recuperation case` WITH
        `teaching seniority in years`           IS 22
        `position fraction`                     IS 1
        `months of work in the year`            IS 10
        `daily price without the cut`           IS 383
        `civil-service daily price without the cut` IS 383
        `form of payment`                       IS `an annual payment`
        `paid in 2009 before June's salary`     IS FALSE
        `budget-pension retiree entitled from the former employer` IS FALSE
        `population`                            IS `government post-primary schools`

-- 12 days at 191.5 ₪.
#ASSERT `recuperation pay in 2009` `a full-position teacher in year 22` EQUALS 2298
#ASSERT `recuperation pay in 2009` `a teacher in a government post-primary school` EQUALS 4596
#ASSERT `recuperation pay reckoned` `a full-position teacher in year 22` `budget-pension payments` EQUALS 4596
#ASSERT `recuperation pay in 2009` `a half-position teacher for ten months` EQUALS 957.5
#ASSERT `recuperation pay for a retiree's year` `a full-position teacher in year 22` 0.5 EQUALS 3447
#ASSERT `the cut part for the period after retirement` `a full-position teacher in year 22` 0.25 EQUALS 574.5
#ASSERT all (GIVEN p YIELD NOT (p EQUALS `any other teaching employee of an owner`)) `the populations outside the circular`
#ASSERT `the jubilee grant` `a teacher who reaches 30 years in March 2009` EQUALS 6000
#ASSERT `the jubilee grant` `a teacher with 25 years of teaching and 31 of work in Israel` EQUALS 0

#TRACE `recuperation pay with June 2009's salary` `a full-position teacher in year 22` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `pay recuperation pay` 2298 AT 10
#TRACE `recuperation pay with June 2009's salary` `a full-position teacher in year 22` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `pay recuperation pay` 2298 AT 11
#TRACE `refund within 60 days` `a full-position teacher in year 22` 0.25 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `pay the cut part for the period after retirement` 574.5 AT 45
#TRACE `the withheld part is never paid` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `pay the withheld part after the determining period` AT 30
#TRACE `the jubilee grant with June's salary` `a teacher who reaches 30 years in March 2009` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `pay the jubilee grant` 6000 AT 10

§§ `Property checks`

-- The circular over its whole finite space: seniority years 1 to 60,
-- positions in quarters from 0 to 1.5, 0 to 12 months of work, day prices
-- from 0 to 600 in steps of 50 with the 2009 price, both kinds of 2010
-- payment's months, a retiree's share of the year in quarters, every
-- population and computation, and a career's seniority on 1 June from 0 to
-- 45 in quarter years.

`both booleans` MEANS LIST TRUE, FALSE
`positions in quarters` MEANS map (GIVEN k YIELD k DIVIDED BY 4) (range 0 6)
`shares in quarters` MEANS LIST 0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1
`the day prices checked` MEANS `the 2009 day price before the cut` FOLLOWED BY map (GIVEN k YIELD k TIMES 50) (range 0 12)
`every population` MEANS
    LIST `State service in official education`, `recognised unofficial kindergartens, primary or middle schools`,
         `colleges of teacher training`, `government post-primary schools`, `any other teaching employee of an owner`
`every computation` MEANS
    LIST `the sum paid to a provident fund, pension fund and study fund included`,
         `income and tax on provident-fund payments in the determining period`, `budget-pension payments`,
         `one-off payments on the end of employment`, `the determining salary for the 2% budget-pension deduction`,
         `any other computation`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, f IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, p IS A NUMBER, e IS A BOOLEAN, r IS A BOOLEAN, w IS A `teaching population`
GIVETH A `recuperation case`
DECIDE `a checked case` n f m p e r w IS
    `recuperation case` WITH
        `teaching seniority in years`           IS n
        `position fraction`                     IS f
        `months of work in the year`            IS m
        `daily price without the cut`           IS p
        `civil-service daily price without the cut` IS 383
        `form of payment`                       IS `an annual payment`
        `paid in 2009 before June's salary`     IS e
        `budget-pension retiree entitled from the former employer` IS r
        `population`                            IS w

-- 1ח: the printed table is a function on years 1 to 60, the BRANCH agrees
-- with it, and the days never fall as the seniority rises.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN n YIELD
                    `the days the table gives for year` n EQUALS LIST (`recuperation days` n)
                AND `recuperation days` n AT MOST `recuperation days` (n PLUS 1))
            (range 1 60)

-- 1ב over the day prices: the cut is half the price and never more than
-- 191.5, the price after it never negative and never falling as the price
-- rises.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN p YIELD
                    `the cut of a day price` p AT MOST p TIMES `the cut rate`
                AND `the cut of a day price` p AT MOST `the most the 2009 cut takes from a day`
                AND `the day price after the cut` p AT LEAST 0
                AND `the day price after the cut` p AT MOST `the day price after the cut` (p PLUS 50))
            `the day prices checked`

-- 1ב-1ז, 1ט-1י, 1יד over every band's first and last year, position,
-- month count, early payment, pensioner and population: the 2009 pay is
-- never negative, never above the uncut pay, cut exactly for an owner's
-- other employee who is no budget pensioner and was not paid early, never
-- falls with a larger position or a month more, and one full position
-- gets as much as any above it.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN n YIELD
                all (GIVEN f YIELD
                        all (GIVEN m YIELD
                                all (GIVEN e YIELD
                                        all (GIVEN r YIELD
                                                all (GIVEN w YIELD
                                                        LET c MEANS `a checked case` n f m 383 e r w
                                                            a MEANS `recuperation pay in 2009` c
                                                            u MEANS `recuperation pay at` 383 `for` c
                                                        IN      a AT LEAST 0
                                                            AND a AT MOST u
                                                            AND (a LESS THAN u) EQUALS (u GREATER THAN 0 AND w EQUALS `any other teaching employee of an owner` AND (NOT r) AND (NOT e))
                                                            AND a AT MOST `recuperation pay in 2009` (`a checked case` n (f PLUS 0.25) m 383 e r w)
                                                            AND a AT MOST `recuperation pay in 2009` (`a checked case` n f (m PLUS 1) 383 e r w)
                                                            AND `recuperation pay in 2009` (`a checked case` n (max f 1) m 383 e r w) EQUALS `recuperation pay in 2009` (`a checked case` n (max f 1 PLUS 0.5) m 383 e r w))
                                                    `every population`)
                                            `both booleans`)
                                    `both booleans`)
                            (LIST 0, 5, 9, 10, 11, 12))
                    `positions in quarters`)
            (LIST 1, 3, 4, 10, 11, 15, 16, 19, 20, 24, 25, 60)

-- 1ו: the two routes agree. A retiree whose year is split before and after
-- the retirement is paid, by 1ו(1), the cut pay for the part before and
-- the full pay for the part after; by 1ו(2), the cut pay with June and the
-- cut part of the time after refunded — the same sum, for every share and
-- every band.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN n YIELD
                all (GIVEN b YIELD
                        LET c MEANS `a checked case` n 1 10 383 FALSE FALSE `any other teaching employee of an owner`
                        IN  `recuperation pay in 2009` c PLUS `the cut part for the period after retirement` c (1 MINUS b)
                            EQUALS `recuperation pay for a retiree's year` c b)
                    `shares in quarters`)
            (LIST 1, 4, 11, 16, 20, 25)

-- 1ג: the 2010 day price for one paid early is never negative and never
-- above the uncut price. 1ד over 0 to 12 months employed in 2009 and each
-- month of 2010: the share paid is nothing or half, never falls as 2010
-- goes on, never rises with more months employed in 2009, and is nothing
-- for one employed all of 2009 and half for one not employed then.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN p YIELD
                LET c MEANS `a checked case` 12 1 10 p TRUE FALSE `any other teaching employee of an owner`
                IN      `the 2010 day price for one paid early in 2009` c AT LEAST 0
                    AND `the 2010 day price for one paid early in 2009` c AT MOST p)
            `the day prices checked`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN e YIELD
                all (GIVEN k YIELD
                        LET x MEANS `share of the 2010 component paid` e k
                        IN      (x EQUALS 0 OR x EQUALS 1 MINUS `the cut rate`)
                            AND ((k EQUALS 12) OR x AT MOST `share of the 2010 component paid` e (k PLUS 1))
                            AND ((e EQUALS 12) OR `share of the 2010 component paid` (e PLUS 1) k AT MOST x)
                            AND ((NOT (e EQUALS 12)) OR x EQUALS 0)
                            AND ((NOT (e EQUALS 0)) OR x EQUALS 1 MINUS `the cut rate`))
                    (range 1 12))
            (range 0 12)

-- 1יא: every listed computation reckons the uncut pay, never less than
-- what is paid; any other computation reckons what is paid.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN o YIELD
                LET c MEANS `a checked case` 22 1 10 383 FALSE FALSE `any other teaching employee of an owner`
                IN      `recuperation pay reckoned` c o AT LEAST `recuperation pay in 2009` c
                    AND (`recuperation pay reckoned` c o EQUALS `recuperation pay in 2009` c) EQUALS (o EQUALS `any other computation`))
            `every computation`

-- 2 on the readings adopted, over a career's seniority on 1 June from 0 to
-- 45 in quarter years: the grant falls in the year the 30 are completed
-- and no other, never above 60% of the determining salary, never falling
-- with a larger position or share of the year.
GIVEN t IS A NUMBER, f IS A NUMBER, s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `jubilee case`
DECIDE `a checked jubilee case` t f s IS
    `jubilee case` WITH
        `teaching seniority set in September 2008`       IS t MINUS 0.75
        `teaching seniority completed by 1 June 2009`    IS t
        `years of work in Israel completed by 1 June 2009` IS t
        `unpaid-leave years with pension rights bought`  IS 0
        `determining salary for pension and severance`   IS 10000
        `jubilee position fraction`                      IS f
        `share of the year employed`                     IS s

#ASSERT all (GIVEN q YIELD
                `entitled to the jubilee grant` (`a checked jubilee case` (q DIVIDED BY 4) 1 1)
                EQUALS (q AT LEAST 120 AND q LESS THAN 124))
            (range 0 180)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN f YIELD
                all (GIVEN s YIELD
                        LET g MEANS `the jubilee grant` (`a checked jubilee case` 30 f s)
                        IN      g AT LEAST 0
                            AND g AT MOST `the jubilee rate` TIMES 10000
                            AND g AT MOST `the jubilee grant` (`a checked jubilee case` 30 (f PLUS 0.25) s)
                            AND g AT MOST `the jubilee grant` (`a checked jubilee case` 30 f (s PLUS 0.25)))
                    `shares in quarters`)
            `positions in quarters`

-- F-2008-09_tashsat_09-e: over the same career, section 2's "30 שנה ומעלה"
-- and the once-only reading part in exactly the years from the 31st on; a
-- teacher in year 35 is in the one and not the other.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN q YIELD
                (NOT (`has the "30 years and more" section 2 names` (`a checked jubilee case` (q DIVIDED BY 4) 1 1)
                      EQUALS `entitled to the jubilee grant` (`a checked jubilee case` (q DIVIDED BY 4) 1 1)))
                EQUALS (q AT LEAST 124))
            (range 0 180)

`"30 years and more" reaches a 35-year teacher, the once-only reading does not` MEANS
        `has the "30 years and more" section 2 names` (`a checked jubilee case` 35 1 1)
    AND NOT `entitled to the jubilee grant` (`a checked jubilee case` 35 1 1)
#ASSERT `"30 years and more" reaches a 35-year teacher, the once-only reading does not`
